REM Package-hosted thread fan-out, runtime proof. `self_fanout_workers::runFanout`
REM spawns two workers from WITHIN that package, naming its own ISOLATED FUNC
REM `bump` by its bare name (plan-115: ISOLATED is the sole marker; plan-81's
REM `self::` spelling was removed in plan-115-B, and this fixture is the evidence
REM that removing the spelling changed no behavior -- the numbers below are the
REM same ones it printed before the conversion).
REM
REM Each worker runs a fresh isolated instance of the package: it sees COUNTER
REM start at its declared 7, mutates only its own arena copy (so the two results
REM are 107 and 207, proving the workers do not share state with each other), and
REM the package instance in this parent thread keeps COUNTER = 7 (proving the
REM worker writes are not shared with the parent). `counter()` read here confirms
REM the parent's 7 once more.

IMPORT io
IMPORT self_fanout_workers

FUNC main AS Integer
  io::print(self_fanout_workers::runFanout())
  io::print("main_counter=" & toString(self_fanout_workers::counter()))
  RETURN 0
END FUNC
